elf-Hosting Machine Requirements","status":"ARCHITECTURE_REQUIREMENTS","derivation_rule":"Architecture -> requirement -> implementation -> direct proof. Benchmarks are downstream and only needed for measured/comparative claims.","laws":[{"id":"KEX-MACH-001","name":"Multi-carrier machine requirement derivation","requirement":"Machine requirements may be demonstrated by workbooks, HTML volumes, compilers, assemblers, WBIOS/BIOS, kernels, emulators, runtimes, servers, network stacks, proof artifacts and executable code. No one carrier is the machine architecture.","proof":"Root manifest classifies each implementation source as a carrier, resident object, machine contract, projection or proof object without elevating a file format to architecture root."},{"id":"KEX-MACH-002","name":"Workbook host closure","requirement":"After the machine capabilities demonstrated by a workbook are instantiated, the machine SHALL be capable of hosting the original workbook as a resident volume using standard file/block, ZIP/OOXML, XML, VFS, memory and projection interfaces."},{"id":"KEX-MACH-003","name":"Recursive self-hosting","requirement":"A KEX machine instance SHALL be capable of hosting the same machine definition and resident volumes required to materialise a successor KEX machine instance. The parent remains the carrier; the child is a successor machine state, not a copy of the physical host."},{"id":"KEX-MACH-004","name":"Reference not duplication","requirement":"Recursive child machines SHOULD inherit resident workbook/HTML resources by logical reference wherever the carrier can preserve the same bytes/state. Recursion SHALL NOT require duplicating every payload at every depth."},{"id":"KEX-MACH-005","name":"Machine contract completeness","requirement":"The recursive host contract SHALL provide truth/state evaluation, firmware/boot, kernel governance, compute/instruction execution, registers, memory, bus/device interfaces, storage, compiler/assembler/loader, networking, display/projection and volume hosting."},{"id":"KEX-SIGNAL-001","name":"Fixed substrate, variable resolution","requirement":"Logical applications, servers, runtimes and projections SHALL resolve through the admitted host compute substrate rather than each implying an independent host CPU pool."},{"id":"KEX-SIGNAL-002","name":"Signal establishes liveness","requirement":"A resident capability becomes live through a valid signal/event/state transition. Residency alone SHALL NOT imply independent execution."},{"id":"KEX-SIGNAL-003","name":"No autonomous recursion","requirement":"Recursive machine materialisation SHALL be event-driven. The artifact SHALL NOT create uncontrolled background depth-generation cycles."},{"id":"KEX-PROJ-001","name":"Global referential visibility","requirement":"The system MAY expose the complete resident topology to the user while keeping actual execution/materialisation dependent on the selected path and its events."},{"id":"KEX-PROJ-002","name":"Conditional executability","requirement":"A visible address or projection SHALL NOT be interpreted as simultaneously executing. Execution is a resolved path through choices, events, state and machine conditions."},{"id":"KEX-PROJ-003","name":"Singular materialisation per frame","requirement":"A projection frame SHALL materialise one resolved projection at a time unless that active projection is itself an explicit window/compositor manager defining child frames."},{"id":"KEX-PROJ-004","name":"Projection successor state","requirement":"Projection changes SHALL be represented as successor state transitions rather than additive rendering of every resident layer into one screen."},{"id":"KEX-NET-001","name":"Single logical ingress","requirement":"The namespace SHALL NOT require one physical public port per logical application, runtime, server, OS or projection."},{"id":"KEX-NET-002","name":"Logical identity over carrier identity","requirement":"Logical addresses SHALL remain authoritative while HTTP/TLS, QUIC, TL/TL1/TL2, VPN-TL, local IPC or other admitted carriers remain replaceable transport/materialisation mechanisms."},{"id":"KEX-NET-003","name":"Capacity classification","requirement":"Carrier-specific resource exhaustion SHALL be recorded as a carrier/materialisation condition, not silently promoted into a KEX namespace limitation."},{"id":"KEX-ZERO-001","name":"Zeroless operative continuity","requirement":"A valid operative state transition SHALL preserve a typed predecessor/successor relation and SHALL NOT require annihilation into an untyped zero/null state."},{"id":"KEX-ZERO-002","name":"Absence is typed","requirement":"Absent, blocked, rejected, rehydratable, resident-not-projected and other non-active conditions SHALL be represented as distinct typed states rather than overloaded as an operative numeric zero."},{"id":"KEX-ZERO-003","name":"Rehydration preserves identity","requirement":"Loss of a material carrier SHALL transition a logical machine/object into an explicit rehydratable/failure state while preserving identity, route and continuation information."},{"id":"KEX-Q-001","name":"Quantum research boundary","requirement":"Zeroless KEX mathematics MAY be developed as a candidate non-null quantum-state grammar, but equivalence with quantum computation SHALL remain a research hypothesis until a formal mapping demonstrates normalization, complex amplitudes/phase, linearity, reversible/unitary evolution, tensor composition, entanglement, measurement/Born statistics and successor-state semantics."},{"id":"KEX-PROOF-001","name":"Direct proof boundary","requirement":"Proof SHALL be attached to the implemented transition/machine contract being claimed. Comparative benchmark evidence SHALL not be used as a prerequisite for defining intrinsic architecture requirements."}],"machine_layers":["truth://tables-and-transition-laws","firmware://wbios-bios","kernel://governance-and-services","isa://instruction-contract","compiler://source-lowering","assembler://encoding","lo